There is no entry of the possession in the revenue record of the State, respondents or its functionaries/ agencies and thus the courts below committed glaring illegality in ignoring the revenue entries showing the possession of the appellants and the entries regarding possession of the plaintiffs/
appellants;
v. That even if there was no evidence of possession of plaintiffs/ appellants, the plaintiffs are deemed to be in possession of the properties on the basis of doctrine of "POSSESSION FOLLOWS TITLE" based upon revenue entries which have been proved in accordance with rule of evidence.

28. The assertion of the Plaintiffs that they were in exclusive possession of the Suit land stands contradicted from their own evidence, particularly from the statements of their witnesses, namely,
PWs Hawali Ram and Talib Hussain; that the spot inspection report and Titima relied upon by the Plaintiffs had not withstood the legal scrutiny and, as such, were not of any help to the Plaintiffs'
cause; that the Plaintiffs' witnesses have put forth contradictory versions as PWs Haweli Ram and Talib Hussain have deposed that the Suit land was under the use and occupation of the Food and Supplies Department till the store was shifted and that the vehicles by which the food grains were brought to the Store used to be parked on the Suit land and the Weighing Scale was also installed there, however, all these important facts were denied specifically by other witnesses of the Plaintiffs;
that the Defendants' assertion that the Suit land was continuously in their use and occupation since the time it was acquired for Labour Sarai finds support from the Plaintiffs evidence as well; that the Defendants' assertion also finds support from the spot inspection report of DW-Mulkh Raj Sharma,
the then Tehsildar, who had given a detailed report regarding whole of the land under Survey Number 85, after physical verification and was assisted in the job by as many as five revenue officials;
CFA No. 24/2005 c/w that the other circumstances which lend support to the case of the Defendants and negated the case of the Plaintiffs are the situation of the Suit land in front of Sarai building and existence of the steps from the Verandah and the water outlets "Parnalas" towards the Suit land in conventional Indian style of construction, inasmuch as, the compound is always in front of the Verandah and had the Suit land been retained by the Plaintiffs, then they would have certainly not allowed nor the Defendants could have kept the Verandah towards the Suit land nor would they have kept it vacant for such a long time.
